Phase 3 of the voice accuracy improvement plan.

Rust side (intent_parser.rs):
- Add KNOWN_REPOS constant (nexus, ultron, servx, zync, ledger-ai, nexus-agent)
- Add fuzzy_match_repo_name() using existing levenshtein() function
- Integrate fuzzy matching into parse_pr_analyse(): if the repo name from
  an exact pattern match isn't a known repo, try fuzzy matching against
  KNOWN_REPOS (threshold: 2 for short repos ≤6 chars, 3 for longer)
- Fuzzy matches return confidence 0.8 and source "fuzzy"
- Add 3 new regex patterns for "the PR" / "the pull request" variants:
  * "the pr <num> in <repo>"
  * "the pr <num> <repo>"
  * "the pull request <num> in <repo>"
- 9 new tests: "the PR" patterns, fuzzy matching (zink→zync, zinc→zync,
  cervix→servx), fuzzy threshold edge cases, confidence verification

Frontend side (recorder.ts):
- Add 5 more PR mishearing corrections: br, be, peer, pee, b r → PR
- Add "the" insertion normalization: "analyse the pr" → "analyse PR"
- Add number-as-words corrections: "two fifty four" → "254", etc.

Tests: 113 Rust tests pass (104 + 9 new), 10 offline command tests pass,
808 frontend modules build.

RAM cost: 0 (fuzzy matching uses existing levenshtein function)

